From aa79c0d68642d503288cf7160bfe13c837490806 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devandroid-bit <180217512+Devandroid-bit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 04:51:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] BACKPORT: f2fs: add block age extent cache and AT_SSR

Backport the S26 in-memory block-age extent cache and connect it to
F2FS allocation and garbage collection. The age tree records the
weighted age and last allocation position of data extents, allowing
new writes to be classified by data temperature instead of only by the
owning file type.

Adapt it to the 4.14 Exynos9820/9825 tree:

- keep the read extent tree and the age extent tree separate so the
  existing read-cache behavior and persistence format are unchanged;
- add the age_extent_cache mount option, which is off by default and
  cannot be switched at remount time;
- add AGE_EXTENT_CACHE memory accounting, shrinker support and
  per-inode runtime initialization/teardown, including zombie trees;
- integrate block-age updates into the outplace data write and file
  truncation paths while preserving the target's 4.14 locking;
- reserve a real CURSEG_ALL_DATA_ATGC slot and use the target curseg
  seg_type to allocate ATGC data without changing the six persistent
  checkpoint logs;
- port AT_SSR victim selection and ATGC segment initialization, save,
  restore and reinitialization around the existing checkpoint and GC
  paths;
- mark pages written by background GC so data allocated for GC is
  routed through ATGC, and clear the marker on completion, retry and
  invalidation paths.

The existing ATGC implementation and gc_merge behavior are retained.
There is no on-disk format change. S26 LFS incompatibility with ATGC is
not imported because the target already permits that combination.

Source: Samsung Galaxy S26 Exynos 2600 kernel 6.12.69, fs/f2fs
(extent_cache.c, segment.c, segment.h, gc.c, checkpoint.c, super.c,
shrinker.c, debug.c and node.c), adapted for Linux 4.14.356.

Signed-off-by: Devandroid-bit <180217512+Devandroid-bit@users.noreply.github.com>

Author: @Devandroid-bit.
